# The approved-package catalog pins a SHA-256 of each package file, and the app
# refuses anything that does not match. GitHub Pages serves the committed bytes,
# so the committed bytes are what the hash describes. Without this, a checkout on
# Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites these files with CRLF, they hash
# differently, and the Load Latest Approved Package button refuses a clone that is
# in fact correct. Pin them to LF so the working copy matches what is served.
packages/*.json text eol=lf
